cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "What if Earth had 2 moons? N-body simulations and a machine-learning surrogate for second-moon stability"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-28
abstract: >-
  N-body simulations of 12,000 hypothetical second moons of Earth, integrated with the real Sun,
  Earth and Moon for up to 100 years, and a Random Forest surrogate that predicts their fate
  (survival, ejection, collision with Earth, or interaction with the Moon) from the initial
  orbital elements.
authors:
  - given-names: "John Rey Ishiguro"
    family-names: "Quizon"
    affiliation: "STI College Legazpi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JreyForFun/two-moons-ml"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - N-body simulation
  - orbital stability
  - natural satellites
  - machine learning
  - REBOUND
